srow(326, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR THE LORD WILL JUDGE HIS PEOPLE" (32:36) — WHEN THE HOLY ONE JUDGES THE NATIONS IT IS JOY BEFORE HIM, AS IT IS SAID "FOR THE LORD WILL JUDGE HIS PEOPLE"; AND WHEN THE HOLY ONE JUDGES ISRAEL IT IS, AS IT WERE, REGRET BEFORE HIM, AS IT IS SAID "AND REPENT HIMSELF FOR HIS SERVANTS" — AND "REPENTING" IS ONLY REGRET: "FOR I REPENT THAT I MADE THEM" (Genesis 6:7), AND "I REPENT THAT I MADE SAUL KING" (1 Samuel 15:11). The head row of piska 326 ({SP_(326, 1, "שמחה", "היא", "לפניו")} "it is joy before Him"; {SP_(326, 1, "כביכול", "תהות", "היא", "לפניו")} "as it were, regret before Him"; {SP_(326, 1, "ואין", "נחמה", "אלא", "תהות")} "and repenting is only regret"): THE VERSE PSALM 135:14 QUOTES WHOLE (the measure\'s find; the Writings\' seat cited never read) read as two judgments — the nations\' with joy, Israel\'s with regret; "repent" (nicham) fixed by Genesis 6:7\'s "I repent that I made them" — the flood prologue\'s own word, the Genesis ledger\'s row; the compile: no law — the verdict\'s two moods (DV32-11). REREAD WHOLE (the Genesis ledger gen_15_flood_prologue — Genesis 6:7).')
srow(326, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN HE SEES THAT THEIR POWER IS GONE" (32:36) — WHEN HE SEES THEIR DESTRUCTION IN THE CAPTIVITY IN WHICH THEY ALL WENT. ({SP_(326, 2, "כשרואה", "כליה", "שלהם", "על", "השביה")} "when He sees their destruction in the captivity"): "their power is gone" (azlat yad, "the hand is gone") read as the captivity\'s annihilation (the translator\'s assonances: gone / annihilation / all of them); no law (DV32-11). Fresh.')
srow(326, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "WHEN HE SEES" — WHEN THEY HAVE DESPAIRED OF THE REDEMPTION. ({SP_(326, 3, "כשנתיאשו", "מן", "הגאלה")} "when they have despaired of the redemption"): the second sign — despair; no law (DV32-11). Fresh.')
srow(326, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "THAT THEIR POWER IS GONE AND THERE IS NONE SHUT UP OR LEFT" — WHEN HE SEES THAT THE SMALLEST COIN IS GONE FROM THE PURSE, AS IT IS SAID "AND WHEN THE BREAKING OF THE POWER OF THE HOLY PEOPLE IS ENDED, ALL THESE SHALL BE FINISHED" (Daniel 12:7). ANOTHER WORD: "WHEN HE SEES THAT THEIR POWER IS GONE" — WHEN HE SEES THAT THERE ARE NONE AMONG THEM WHO SEEK MERCY FOR THEM LIKE MOSES, AS IT IS SAID "AND HE SAID HE WOULD DESTROY THEM, HAD NOT MOSES HIS CHOSEN" (Psalm 106:23). ({SP_(326, 4, "כשרואה", "שתכלה", "פרוטה", "מן", "הכיס")} "when He sees that the smallest coin is gone from the purse"; {SP_(326, 4, "שמבקשים", "עליהם", "רחמים", "כמשה")} "who seek mercy for them like Moses"): the third and fourth signs — the last coin (perutah, "the smallest coin") gone, no one to plead like Moses (the calf\'s intercession, Exodus 32:11 on the tape — a RUN CITATION; Psalm 106:23 the Writings\' seat cited); no law (DV32-11). Fresh.')
srow(326, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "WHEN HE SEES" — WHEN HE SEES THAT THERE ARE NONE AMONG THEM WHO SEEK MERCY FOR THEM LIKE AARON, AS IT IS SAID "AND HE STOOD BETWEEN THE DEAD AND THE LIVING, AND THE PLAGUE WAS STAYED" (Numbers 17:13). ({SP_(326, 5, "רחמים", "כאהרן")} "mercy like Aaron"): Aaron\'s incense between the dead and the living (Numbers 17:13 on the tape — a RUN CITATION); no law (DV32-11). Fresh.')
srow(326, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "WHEN HE SEES" — WHEN HE SEES THAT THERE ARE NONE AMONG THEM WHO SEEK MERCY FOR THEM LIKE PHINEHAS, AS IT IS SAID "THEN STOOD UP PHINEHAS AND PRAYED" (Psalm 106:30). ({SP_(326, 6, "רחמים", "כפינחס")} "mercy like Phinehas"): Phinehas\'s act (Numbers 25:7-8 on the tape — a RUN CITATION) read as prayer by the Psalm\'s "and prayed" (vayefalel; the Writings\' seat cited); no law (DV32-11). Fresh.')
srow(326, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "WHEN HE SEES THAT THEIR POWER IS GONE AND THERE IS NONE SHUT UP OR LEFT" — NONE SHUT UP AND NONE LEFT, AND THERE IS NO HELPER FOR ISRAEL. ({SP_(326, 7, "ואין", "עוזר", "לישראל")} "and there is no helper for Israel"): "none" (efes) doubled — the last row of the piska; no law (DV32-11). Fresh.')
srow(327, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE SHALL SAY: WHERE ARE THEIR GODS" (32:37) — R. YEHUDAH EXPOUNDS IT OF ISRAEL, AND R. NECHEMIAH EXPOUNDS IT OF THE NATIONS OF THE WORLD. The head row of piska 327 ({SP_(327, 1, "ורבי", "נחמיה", "דורשו", "כלפי", "אמות", "העולם")} "and R. Nechemiah expounds it of the nations of the world"): the two-reading frame a third time (322, 323, 327); no law (DV32-11). Fresh.')
srow(327, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. YEHUDAH SAYS: ISRAEL ARE TO SAY TO THE NATIONS OF THE WORLD: WHERE ARE YOUR CONSULS AND YOUR GOVERNORS? ({SP_(327, 2, "היכן", "הפיטקים", "והגמונים", "שלכם")} "where are your consuls and governors"): THE ROMAN LEXICON AGAIN (317:5\'s officers) — the last row of the piska: R. Yehudah\'s reading alone stands here, R. Nechemiah\'s follows as 328:2 (Titus); no law (DV32-11). Fresh.')
srow(328, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHO ATE THE FAT OF THEIR SACRIFICES" (32:38) — THAT WE GAVE THEM PROVISIONS AND MADE THEM DONATIVES AND BROUGHT THEM UP SALARIES. The head row of piska 328 ({SP_(328, 1, "שהיינו", "נותנים", "להם", "אפסניות")} "that we gave them provisions"): THE MISPRINTED HEAD — the Hebrew marker reads 32:35 while the words are 32:38\'s (the English true; the row seated by its words — sitting 19\'s lesson 1, the ink\'s first-pass fall); the army\'s allowances in Hebrew letters (the translator: Rome\'s annona, donativa and salaria — "provisions, donatives, salt-money"); the sacrifices\' fat the tax; no law (DV32-11). Fresh.')
srow(328, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"LET THEM RISE UP AND HELP YOU" (32:38) — "LET THEM RISE UP AND HELP YOU" WITH THE FULL PLURAL IS NOT WRITTEN HERE, BUT "LET THEM RISE UP AND HELP YOU" WITH THE SUFFIX. R. NECHEMIAH SAYS: THIS IS THE WICKED TITUS, THE SON OF VESPASIAN\'S WIFE, WHO ENTERED THE HOLY OF HOLIES AND CUT THE TWO CURTAINS WITH A SWORD AND SAID: IF HE IS GOD, LET HIM COME AND PROTEST. ({SP_(328, 2, "זה", "טיטוס", "הרשע")} "this is the wicked Titus"; {SP_(328, 2, "אם", "אלוה", "הוא", "יבוא", "וימחה")} "if He is God let Him come and protest"): THE WRITTEN FORM\'S DEFECTIVE SUFFIX (the translator: the letter vav omitted, a singular "let Him help you" possible — the ketiv the parser\'s form); Titus in the sanctuary (the translator: Avot deRabbi Natan B 7; the testing shelf not opened); no law (DV32-11). Fresh.')
srow(328, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHO ATE THE FAT OF THEIR SACRIFICES" — HE SAID: MOSES LED THESE ASTRAY AND SAID TO THEM, BUILD YOU AN ALTAR AND OFFER ON IT BURNT OFFERINGS AND POUR ON IT LIBATIONS, AS IN THE MATTER SAID "THE ONE LAMB YOU SHALL OFFER IN THE MORNING AND THE SECOND LAMB YOU SHALL OFFER AT DUSK" (Numbers 28:4). ({SP_(328, 3, "הללו", "משה", "הטעם")} "Moses led these astray"; {SP_(328, 3, "בנו", "לכם", "מזבח")} "build you an altar"): the speaker unnamed in the Hebrew (the translator follows Hammer and Neusner: Titus); the daily offering (Numbers 28:4, compiled at Numbers — a REFERENCE) the mocker\'s example; no law (DV32-11). Fresh.')
srow(328, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"LET THEM RISE UP AND HELP YOU, LET THEM BE YOUR PROTECTION" (32:38) — FOR EVERYTHING THE HOLY ONE PARDONS; FOR THE PROFANATION OF THE NAME HE EXACTS AT ONCE. ({SP_(328, 4, "על", "הכל", "הקדוש", "ברוך", "הוא", "מוחל")} "for everything the Holy One pardons"; {SP_(328, 4, "על", "חלול", "השם", "פורע", "מיד")} "for the profanation of the Name He exacts at once"): A RULE FROM THE VERSE — the profanation of the Name punished at once, all else pardoned (the last row of the piska; Yoma 86a\'s divisions the testing shelf, not opened); the compile: a status the daemon may write — the Name profaned, the exaction immediate (DV32-11). Fresh.')
srow(329, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"SEE NOW THAT I, I AM HE" (32:39) — THIS IS THE ANSWER TO THOSE WHO SAY THERE IS NO AUTHORITY IN HEAVEN; TO ONE WHO SAYS THERE ARE TWO AUTHORITIES IN HEAVEN THEY ANSWER AND SAY: IS IT NOT ALREADY WRITTEN "AND THERE IS NO GOD WITH ME"? OR IS IT AS ONE WHO HAS NO POWER TO KILL OR TO MAKE ALIVE, TO DO EVIL OR TO DO GOOD? THE TEACHING SAYS "SEE NOW THAT I, I AM HE; I KILL AND I MAKE ALIVE", AND IT SAYS "THUS SAYS THE LORD, THE KING OF ISRAEL AND HIS REDEEMER, THE LORD OF HOSTS: I AM THE FIRST AND I AM THE LAST, AND BESIDE ME THERE IS NO GOD" (Isaiah 44:6). The head row of piska 329 ({SP_(329, 1, "זו", "תשובה", "לאומרים", "אין", "רשות", "בשמים")} "this is the answer to those who say there is no authority in Heaven"; {SP_(329, 1, "האומר", "שתי", "רשויות", "בשמים")} "one who says there are two authorities in Heaven"): THE TWO POWERS REFUTED by the doubled "I" and by "no god with Me" (the translator: Mekhilta Shirah 4\'s parallel); the compile: the unity the tape carries from 6:4 — a status reaffirmed, no new law (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(329, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "I KILL AND I MAKE ALIVE" (32:39) — THIS IS ONE OF FOUR PROMISES THAT WERE GIVEN THEM AS A HINT OF THE RESURRECTION OF THE DEAD. ({SP_(329, 2, "זה", "אחד", "מארבע", "הבטחות")} "this is one of four promises"; {SP_(329, 2, "רמז", "לתחית", "המתים")} "a hint of the resurrection of the dead"): the four listed in 329:3; no law (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(329, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"I KILL AND I MAKE ALIVE"; "LET MY SOUL DIE THE DEATH OF THE UPRIGHT" (Numbers 23:10); "LET REUBEN LIVE AND NOT DIE" (33:6); "HE WILL REVIVE US AFTER TWO DAYS" (Hosea 6:2) — I MIGHT HEAR DEATH IN ONE AND LIFE IN ANOTHER; THE TEACHING SAYS "I HAVE WOUNDED AND I HEAL" — AS THE WOUND AND THE HEALING ARE IN ONE, SO DEATH AND LIFE ARE IN ONE. ({SP_(329, 3, "שומע", "אני", "מיתה", "באחד", "וחיים", "באחד")} "I might hear death in one and life in another"; {SP_(329, 3, "כך", "מיתה", "וחיים", "באחד")} "so death and life are in one"): THE FOUR PROMISES — Balaam\'s (Numbers 23:10 on the tape, a RUN CITATION), the blessing\'s 33:6 (THE NEXT CHAPTER\'S — the seat cited, the piska not opened), Hosea\'s (the Prophets\' seat cited), the song\'s; "wounded and heal" the analogy that puts death and life in one body; the Hebrew marker "Deuteronomy 33" without the verse; no law (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(329, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THERE IS NONE THAT DELIVERS OUT OF MY HAND" (32:39) — FATHERS DO NOT DELIVER SONS: ABRAHAM DOES NOT DELIVER ISHMAEL, NOR ISAAC ESAU; I HAVE ONLY FATHERS WHO DO NOT DELIVER SONS — BROTHERS FOR BROTHERS, WHENCE? THE TEACHING SAYS "NO MAN CAN BY ANY MEANS REDEEM HIS BROTHER" (Psalm 49:8) — ISAAC DOES NOT DELIVER ISHMAEL, NOR JACOB ESAU; AND EVEN IF A MAN GIVES ALL THE MONEY IN THE WORLD THEY DO NOT GIVE HIM HIS RANSOM, AS IT IS SAID "NO MAN CAN BY ANY MEANS REDEEM HIS BROTHER … FOR THE REDEMPTION OF THEIR SOUL IS COSTLY" — THIS SOUL IS PRECIOUS: WHEN A MAN SINS WITH IT THERE IS NO PAYMENT FOR IT. ({SP_(329, 4, "אין", "אבות", "מצילים", "את", "הבנים")} "fathers do not deliver sons"; {SP_(329, 4, "אחים", "את", "אחים", "מנין")} "brothers for brothers, whence"; {SP_(329, 4, "יקרה", "היא", "נפש", "זו")} "this soul is precious"): NO RANSOM FOR A SOUL — the fathers and brothers named from the tape (Abraham and Ishmael, Isaac and Esau, Jacob and Esau — RUN CITATIONS); the ransom (kofer, "a payment for a life") of Exodus 21:30 compiled at Exodus — a REFERENCE, here denied for the soul; the last row of the piska; the compile: no law (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(330, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR I LIFT UP MY HAND TO HEAVEN" (32:40) — WHEN THE HOLY ONE CREATED THE WORLD HE CREATED IT ONLY BY A WORD, AND HE CREATED IT ONLY BY AN OATH; AND WHO CAUSED HIM TO SWEAR? THOSE LACKING FAITH CAUSED HIM TO SWEAR, AS IT IS SAID "AND HE LIFTED UP HIS HAND TO THEM, TO OVERTHROW THEM IN THE WILDERNESS" (Psalm 106:26), AND "I HAVE LIFTED UP MY HAND TO THE NATIONS" (Ezekiel 36:7). The head row of piska 330 ({SP_(330, 1, "לא", "בראו", "אלא", "במאמר")} "He created it only by a word"; {SP_(330, 1, "מחסרי", "אמנה", "הם", "גרמו", "לו", "לשבע")} "those lacking faith caused Him to swear"): THE LIFTED HAND IS THE OATH — the spies\' generation\'s oath (Numbers 14:28-30 on the tape, a RUN CITATION; Psalm 106:26 the Writings\' seat cited) the cause; the world by utterance (the translator: Mishnah Avot 5:1\'s ten utterances — the testing shelf not opened); Onkelos\'s "the house of My Shekhinah in heaven" (the measure) the same lifted hand; the compile: no law — the oath\'s formula (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(330, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SAY: AS I LIVE FOR EVER" (32:40) — NOT AS THE MEASURE OF FLESH AND BLOOD IS THE MEASURE OF THE HOLY ONE: THE MEASURE OF FLESH AND BLOOD — A GOVERNOR ENTERS HIS PROVINCE; IF HE CAN EXACT FROM HIS PREDECESSOR HE EXACTS, AND IF NOT HE CANNOT EXACT; BUT HE WHO SPOKE AND THE WORLD WAS IS NOT SO — IF HE DOES NOT EXACT FROM THE LIVING HE EXACTS FROM THE DEAD, IF HE DOES NOT EXACT IN THIS WORLD HE EXACTS IN THE WORLD TO COME. ({SP_(330, 2, "שלא", "כמדת", "בשר", "ודם", "מדת", "הקדוש", "ברוך")} "not as the measure of flesh and blood is the measure of the Holy One"; {SP_(330, 2, "אינו", "נפרע", "מן", "החיים", "נפרע", "מן", "המתים")} "if He does not exact from the living He exacts from the dead"): "AS I LIVE FOR EVER" — the governor\'s term against the eternal Judge (the lexicon of 317:5 — the governor, the province); the exaction from the dead and in the world to come; the last row of the piska; no law (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(331, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"IF I WHET MY GLITTERING SWORD" (32:41) — WHEN PUNISHMENT GOES OUT FROM BEFORE ME IT IS SWIFT AS LIGHTNING; EVEN SO — "AND MY HAND TAKE HOLD ON JUDGMENT". The head row of piska 331 ({SP_(331, 1, "קלה", "היא", "כברק")} "it is swift as lightning"): "glittering" (barak, "lightning") the pun; judgment held even in haste (the translator: Mekhilta Shirah 4); no law (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(331, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"I WILL RENDER VENGEANCE TO MY ADVERSARIES" — THAT IS ONE; "AND WILL RECOMPENSE THOSE WHO HATE ME" — THAT IS TWO. ({SP_(331, 2, "הרי", "אחד")} "that is one"; {SP_(331, 2, "הרי", "שנים")} "that is two"): the two vengeances counted (333:3 names them — the blood and the violence); the translator: the small-type text an interpolation (Finkelstein); no law (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(331, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "I WILL RENDER VENGEANCE TO MY ADVERSARIES" — THESE ARE THE CUTHEANS (THE SAMARITANS), AS IT IS SAID "AND THE ADVERSARIES OF JUDAH AND BENJAMIN HEARD" (Ezra 4:1). ({SP_(331, 3, "אלו", "כותיים")} "these are the Cutheans"): the Samaritans (kutim, "the Cutheans") — the Writings\' seat Ezra 4:1 cited, never read; no law (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(331, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND WILL RECOMPENSE THOSE WHO HATE ME" — THESE ARE THE SECTARIANS; AND SO IT SAYS "DO I NOT HATE THEM, O LORD, WHO HATE YOU, AND STRIVE WITH THOSE WHO RISE UP AGAINST YOU" (Psalm 139:21). ({SP_(331, 4, "אלו", "המינים")} "these are the sectarians"): the sectarians (minim, "the sectarians") — 320:8\'s again; the last row of the piska; the translator: Avot deRabbi Natan A 16; no law (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(332, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"I WILL MAKE MY ARROWS DRUNK WITH BLOOD" (32:42) — AND CAN ARROWS BE DRUNK WITH BLOOD? RATHER, I MAKE OTHERS DRUNK WITH WHAT MY ARROWS DO. The head row of piska 332 ({SP_(332, 1, "וכי", "אפשר", "להם", "לחצים", "שישתכרו", "מדם")} "can arrows be drunk with blood"): the figure resolved by the causative — "I make others drunk"; no law (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(332, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND MY SWORD SHALL DEVOUR FLESH" (32:42) — AND CAN A SWORD DEVOUR FLESH? RATHER, I FEED OTHERS WITH WHAT MY SWORD DOES; AND SO IT SAYS "AND YOU, SON OF MAN, SAY TO THE BIRDS OF EVERY WING" (Ezekiel 39:17), AND IT SAYS "AND YOU SHALL EAT FAT TILL YOU ARE FULL AND DRINK BLOOD", AND "YOU SHALL EAT THE FLESH OF THE MIGHTY", AND "YOU SHALL BE FILLED AT MY TABLE WITH HORSES AND CHARIOTS", AND IT SAYS "THE SWORD OF THE LORD IS FILLED WITH BLOOD, IT IS MADE FAT WITH FATNESS" (Isaiah 34:6) — WHY? "FOR THE LORD HAS A SACRIFICE IN BOZRAH AND A GREAT SLAUGHTER IN THE LAND OF EDOM". ({SP_(332, 2, "הריני", "מאכיל", "אחרים")} "I feed others"; {SP_(332, 2, "כי", "זבח", "לה", "בבצרה")} "for the LORD has a sacrifice in Bozrah"): the feast of Gog (Ezekiel 39:17-20) and Edom\'s slaughter (Isaiah 34:6) the sword\'s eaters — the Prophets\' seats cited, never read; the assonance sacrifice / slaughter (zevach / tevach) the translator\'s; no law (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(332, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"WITH THE BLOOD OF THE SLAIN AND THE CAPTIVES" (32:42) — FOR WHAT THEY DID TO THE SLAIN OF MY PEOPLE; AND SO IT SAYS "OH THAT MY HEAD WERE WATERS AND MY EYES A FOUNTAIN OF TEARS, THAT I MIGHT WEEP DAY AND NIGHT FOR THE SLAIN OF THE DAUGHTER OF MY PEOPLE" (Jeremiah 8:23). ({SP_(332, 3, "ממה", "שעשו", "בחללי", "עמי")} "for what they did to the slain of My people"): the slain (chalal, "one pierced") of the verse the nations\' victims; no law (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(332, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE CAPTIVES" — FOR WHAT THEY DID TO THE CAPTIVES OF MY PEOPLE; AND SO IT SAYS "AND THEY SHALL TAKE THEM CAPTIVE WHOSE CAPTIVES THEY WERE, AND SHALL RULE OVER THEIR OPPRESSORS" (Isaiah 14:2). ({SP_(332, 4, "ממה", "שעשו", "בשבי", "עמי")} "for what they did to the captives of My people"): the captives\' turn (the Prophets\' seat cited); no law (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(332, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"FROM THE HEAD OF THE LEADERS OF THE ENEMY" (32:42) — WHEN THE HOLY ONE BRINGS PUNISHMENT ON THE NATIONS HE BRINGS UPON THEM NOT THEIRS ALONE BUT THEIRS AND THEIR FATHERS\' FROM NIMROD ONWARD; WHEN HE BRINGS GOOD ON ISRAEL HE BRINGS UPON THEM THEIRS AND THEIR FATHERS\' FROM ABRAHAM ONWARD. ({SP_(332, 5, "שלהם", "ושל", "אבותיהם", "מנמרוד", "ואילך")} "theirs and their fathers from Nimrod onward"; {SP_(332, 5, "מאברהם", "ואילך")} "from Abraham onward"): NIMROD AND ABRAHAM THE TWO HEADS of the two ledgers — the fathers\' deeds reckoned to the sons both ways (Genesis 10:8 and 12:1 on the tape, RUN CITATIONS); no law (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(332, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "FROM THE HEAD OF THE LEADERS OF THE ENEMY" — WHY DID THEY SEE FIT TO HANG ALL THE PUNISHMENTS ON PHARAOH\'S HEAD? BECAUSE HE WAS THE FIRST TO ENSLAVE ISRAEL. ({SP_(332, 6, "מפני", "שהיה", "תחלה", "לשעבודם", "של", "ישראל")} "because he was the first to enslave Israel"): "leaders" (par\'ot) read as Pharaoh (par\'oh) — Exodus 1:8-11 on the tape a RUN CITATION; the last row of the piska; no law (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(333, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"SING ALOUD, O NATIONS, OF HIS PEOPLE" (32:43) — TOMORROW, WHEN THE HOLY ONE BRINGS REDEMPTION TO ISRAEL, THE NATIONS OF THE WORLD TREMBLE BEFORE HIM; AND THIS IS NOT THEIR FIRST TIME, FOR THEY TREMBLED OF OLD, AS IN THE MATTER SAID "THE PEOPLES HEARD, THEY TREMBLE" (Exodus 15:14). The head row of piska 333 ({SP_(333, 1, "אמות", "העולם", "מתרגזים", "לפניו")} "the nations of the world tremble before Him"; {SP_(333, 1, "שכבר", "רגזו", "מקדם")} "for they trembled of old"): THE TWO SONGS JOINED — the Song at the Sea (Exodus 15:14 on the tape, a RUN CITATION) the first trembling, the redemption\'s the second (the translator: Mekhilta Shirah 9); no law (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(333, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "SING ALOUD, O NATIONS, OF HIS PEOPLE" — THE NATIONS OF THE WORLD ARE TO PRAISE BEFORE ISRAEL, AS IT IS SAID "SING ALOUD, O NATIONS, OF HIS PEOPLE"; AND EVEN HEAVEN AND EARTH, AS IT IS SAID "SING, O HEAVENS, FOR THE LORD HAS DONE IT; SHOUT, YOU LOWER PARTS OF THE EARTH" (Isaiah 44:23); WHENCE EVEN THE MOUNTAINS AND HILLS? "THE MOUNTAINS AND THE HILLS SHALL BREAK FORTH BEFORE YOU INTO SINGING" (Isaiah 55:12); WHENCE EVEN THE TREES? "AND ALL THE TREES OF THE FIELD SHALL CLAP THEIR HANDS" (Isaiah 55:12); WHENCE EVEN THE FATHERS AND THE MOTHERS? "LET THE INHABITANTS OF THE ROCK SING, LET THEM SHOUT FROM THE TOP OF THE MOUNTAINS" (Isaiah 42:11). ({SP_(333, 2, "עתידים", "אמות", "העולם", "להיות", "מקלסים", "לפני", "ישראל")} "the nations of the world are to praise before Israel"; {SP_(333, 2, "מנין", "אף", "אבות", "ואמהות")} "whence even the fathers and mothers"): THE WITNESSES OF 32:1 CALLED TO THE PRAISE — heaven and earth (the song\'s frame closing on its openers), then the mountains, the trees, the fathers and mothers ("the inhabitants of the rock" — the tombs); the Prophets\' seats cited; the English\'s Isaiah 43:11 a misprint for the Hebrew\'s 42:11; no law (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(333, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR HE WILL AVENGE THE BLOOD OF HIS SERVANTS, AND RENDER VENGEANCE TO HIS ADVERSARIES" (32:43) — TWO VENGEANCES: VENGEANCE FOR THE BLOOD AND VENGEANCE FOR THE VIOLENCE; WHENCE THAT ALL THE VIOLENCE THE NATIONS OF THE WORLD DID TO ISRAEL IS RECKONED TO THEM AS IF THEY SHED INNOCENT BLOOD? AS IT IS SAID "I WILL GATHER ALL THE NATIONS AND BRING THEM DOWN TO THE VALLEY OF JEHOSHAPHAT, AND PLEAD WITH THEM THERE FOR MY PEOPLE ISRAEL" (Joel 4:2), "EGYPT SHALL BE A DESOLATION AND EDOM A DESOLATE WILDERNESS, FOR THE VIOLENCE AGAINST THE CHILDREN OF JUDAH, BECAUSE THEY SHED INNOCENT BLOOD IN THEIR LAND" (Joel 4:19); AT THAT HOUR, "JUDAH SHALL DWELL FOR EVER AND JERUSALEM FROM GENERATION TO GENERATION, AND I WILL HOLD THEIR BLOOD INNOCENT WHICH I HAVE NOT HELD INNOCENT, AND THE LORD DWELLS IN ZION" (Joel 4:20-21). ({SP_(333, 3, "שתי", "נקמות", "נקם", "על", "הדם", "ונקם", "על")} "two vengeances: vengeance for the blood and vengeance for"; {SP_(333, 3, "כאלו", "דם", "נקי", "שפכו")} "as if they shed innocent blood"): VIOLENCE RECKONED AS BLOODSHED — the two vengeances of 331:2 named; the Prophets\' seats cited, never read; the compile: no law — the equation a rule of reckoning, the tape\'s "innocent blood" formula (19:10, 21:8) a REFERENCE (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(333, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HIS LAND MAKES ATONEMENT FOR HIS PEOPLE" (32:43) — WHENCE THAT THE KILLING OF ISRAEL BY THE NATIONS OF THE WORLD IS AN ATONEMENT FOR THEM IN THE WORLD TO COME? AS IT IS SAID "A PSALM OF ASAPH: O GOD, THE NATIONS HAVE COME INTO YOUR INHERITANCE … THEY HAVE GIVEN THE DEAD BODIES OF YOUR SERVANTS … THEY HAVE SHED THEIR BLOOD LIKE WATER" (Psalm 79:1-3). ANOTHER WORD: WHENCE DO YOU SAY THAT THE DESCENT OF THE WICKED TO GEHENNA (THE PLACE OF PUNISHMENT) IS AN ATONEMENT FOR THEM? "I HAVE GIVEN EGYPT AS YOUR RANSOM, ETHIOPIA AND SEBA FOR YOU; SINCE YOU ARE PRECIOUS IN MY SIGHT AND HONORED, AND I HAVE LOVED YOU" (Isaiah 43:3-4). R. MEIR USED TO SAY: WHOEVER DWELLS IN THE LAND OF ISRAEL, THE LAND OF ISRAEL ATONES FOR HIM, AS IT IS SAID "THE PEOPLE WHO DWELL IN IT ARE FORGIVEN INIQUITY" (Isaiah 33:24) — STILL THE MATTER HANGS ON WHAT IS NOT SETTLED: WE DO NOT KNOW WHETHER THEY UNLOAD THEIR INIQUITIES ON IT OR BEAR THEIR INIQUITIES ON IT; WHEN IT SAYS "AND HIS LAND MAKES ATONEMENT FOR HIS PEOPLE" — THEY UNLOAD THEIR INIQUITIES ON IT AND DO NOT BEAR THEIR INIQUITIES ON IT. AND SO R. MEIR USED TO SAY: WHOEVER DWELLS IN THE LAND OF ISRAEL AND READS THE SHEMA (HEAR, O ISRAEL) MORNING AND EVENING AND SPEAKS THE HOLY TONGUE IS A SON OF THE WORLD TO COME. ({SP_(333, 4, "כל", "היושב", "בארץ", "ישראל", "ארץ", "ישראל", "מכפרת")} "whoever dwells in the land of Israel, the land of Israel atones"; {SP_(333, 4, "וקורא", "קריאת", "שמע", "שחרית", "וערבית")} "and reads the Shema morning and evening"; {SP_(333, 4, "ומדבר", "בלשון", "הקדש")} "and speaks the holy tongue"): A RULE FROM THE VERSE — THE LAND ATONES (R. Meir), its condition settled by the verse (the iniquities unloaded, not borne); the Shema\'s morning and evening (6:7\'s "when you lie down and when you rise", compiled at chapter 6 — a REFERENCE; Mishnah Berakhot 1:1 the answer sheet\'s clock, not opened) and the holy tongue the world to come\'s conditions; the death by the nations an atonement, Gehenna the wicked\'s; the compile: a status — dwelling in the land, the Shema twice, the tongue (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(333, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'YOU SAY: GREAT IS THIS SONG, FOR IT HAS IN IT THE PRESENT, AND IT HAS IN IT THE PAST, AND IT HAS IN IT THE FUTURE TO COME, AND IT HAS IN IT THIS WORLD, AND IT HAS IN IT THE WORLD TO COME. ({SP_(333, 5, "גדולה", "שירה", "זו")} "great is this song"; {SP_(333, 5, "ויש", "בה", "לעתיד", "לבוא")} "and it has in it the future to come"): THE SONG\'S THREE TIMES AND TWO WORLDS — the spine\'s own verdict on the song\'s tense: the past the tape\'s (the desert, the eagle, the honey), the present the charge\'s, the future a POINTER (the vengeance, the nations\' song) — THE RETELLING RULES\' three kinds in the tradition\'s words; the last row of the song\'s piskaot (306-333 on 32:1-43); no law (DV32-12). Fresh.')
srow(334, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND MOSES CAME" (32:44) — IT IS SAID HERE "AND MOSES CAME" AND IT IS SAID THERE "AND MOSES WENT" (31:1); ONE CANNOT SAY "AND MOSES CAME" SINCE "AND MOSES WENT" IS ALREADY SAID, AND ONE CANNOT SAY "AND MOSES WENT" SINCE "AND MOSES CAME" IS ALREADY SAID — SAY FROM NOW: HIS SUCCESSOR CAME, AND THE AUTHORITY WAS GIVEN INTO ANOTHER\'S HAND. The head row of piska 334 ({SP_(334, 1, "נאמר", "כאן", "ויבא", "משה")} "it is said here: and Moses came"; {SP_(334, 1, "בא", "דיותיכוס", "שלו")} "his successor came"; {SP_(334, 1, "והרשות", "נתנה", "ביד", "אחר")} "and the authority was given into another\'s hand"): 31:1\'S "AND MOSES WENT" — sitting 19\'s row (the marker\'s day, the ledger deu_29_31) read against 32:44\'s "came": the successor (diadochos, "the one who takes over" — the Greek in Hebrew letters; the translator) arrives and the authority passes; the compile: the aftermath\'s frame — Joshua\'s authority the status the tape set at 31:14-23\'s commission, no new law (DV32A-01). REREAD WHOLE (sitting 19\'s reading — 31:1; the ledger deu_29_31).')
srow(334, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SPOKE ALL THE WORDS OF THIS SONG IN THE EARS OF THE PEOPLE" (32:44) — THIS TEACHES THAT HE SANK THEM INTO THEIR EARS. ({SP_(334, 2, "מלמד", "שהיה", "משקעם", "באזניהם")} "this teaches that he sank them into their ears"): the manner of the speaking; no law (DV32A-01). Fresh.')
srow(334, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE AND HOSHEA SON OF NUN" (32:44) — WHY DO I NEED IT? IS IT NOT ALREADY SAID "AND MOSES CALLED HOSHEA SON OF NUN JOSHUA" (Numbers 13:16)? WHAT DOES THE TEACHING SAY BY "HE AND HOSHEA SON OF NUN"? TO MAKE KNOWN JOSHUA\'S RIGHTEOUSNESS — I MIGHT HEAR THAT HIS MIND GREW PROUD OVER HIM WHEN HE WAS APPOINTED TO AUTHORITY; THE TEACHING SAYS "HE AND HOSHEA SON OF NUN": HOSHEA IN HIS RIGHTEOUSNESS — THOUGH APPOINTED LEADER OVER ISRAEL, HE IS HOSHEA IN HIS RIGHTEOUSNESS. LIKEWISE YOU SAY "AND JOSEPH WAS IN EGYPT" (Exodus 1:5) — DO WE NOT KNOW THAT JOSEPH WAS IN EGYPT? RATHER, TO MAKE KNOWN JOSEPH\'S RIGHTEOUSNESS, WHO SHEPHERDED HIS FATHER\'S FLOCK, AND THOUGH APPOINTED KING IN EGYPT HE IS JOSEPH IN HIS RIGHTEOUSNESS. LIKEWISE "AND DAVID WAS THE YOUNGEST" (1 Samuel 17:14) — DO WE NOT KNOW THAT DAVID WAS THE YOUNGEST? RATHER, TO MAKE KNOWN TO YOU DAVID\'S RIGHTEOUSNESS, WHO SHEPHERDED HIS FATHER\'S FLOCK, AND THOUGH APPOINTED KING OVER ISRAEL HE IS DAVID IN HIS LITTLENESS. ({SP_(334, 3, "להודיע", "צדקו", "של", "יהושע")} "to make known Joshua\'s righteousness"; {SP_(334, 3, "הוא", "הושע", "בצדקו")} "he is Hoshea in his righteousness"; {SP_(334, 3, "הוא", "דוד", "בקטנו")} "he is David in his littleness"): THE OLD NAME KEPT — the measure\'s kin (Numbers 13:16, the spies\' renaming on the tape: shelach.spies\' joshua_name a RUN CITATION) read as humility unchanged by office; Joseph and David the parallels (Exodus 1:5 on the tape; the Prophets\' seat cited); the last row of the piska; no law (DV32A-01). Fresh.')
srow(335, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE SAID TO THEM: SET YOUR HEART TO ALL THE WORDS WHICH I TESTIFY AGAINST YOU THIS DAY" (32:46) — A MAN MUST HAVE HIS HEART, HIS EYES AND HIS EARS DIRECTED TO THE WORDS OF TORAH; AND SO IT SAYS "SON OF MAN, SEE WITH YOUR EYES AND HEAR WITH YOUR EARS ALL THAT I SAY TO YOU, AND SET YOUR HEART TO THE ENTRANCE OF THE HOUSE" (Ezekiel 44:5); AN ARGUMENT FROM THE LIGHTER: IF THE TEMPLE, WHICH IS SEEN WITH THE EYES AND MEASURED BY THE HAND, NEEDS A MAN\'S HEART, EYES AND EARS DIRECTED, THE WORDS OF TORAH, WHICH ARE LIKE MOUNTAINS HANGING BY A HAIR — HOW MUCH MORE. The head row of piska 335 ({SP_(335, 1, "צריך", "אדם", "להיות", "לבו", "ועיניו", "ואזניו", "מכונים")} "a man must have his heart, eyes and ears directed"; {SP_(335, 1, "כהררים", "התלויים", "בשערה")} "like mountains hanging by a hair"): THE CHARGE\'S MANNER — heart, eyes and ears; "mountains hanging by a hair" Mishnah Chagigah 1:8\'s phrase for the laws with scant Scripture (317:3 named it; the testing shelf not opened); the Hebrew marker Ezekiel 40:4 for words that are 44:5\'s (the English\'s citation; the Prophets\' seat cited); the compile: no law — the charge\'s attention (DV32A-02). Fresh.')
srow(335, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHICH YOU SHALL COMMAND YOUR CHILDREN TO OBSERVE" (32:46) — HE SAID TO THEM: I MUST BE GRATEFUL TO YOU THAT YOU WILL UPHOLD THE TORAH AFTER ME; YOU TOO MUST BE GRATEFUL TO YOUR CHILDREN THAT THEY WILL UPHOLD THE TORAH AFTER YOU. IT HAPPENED THAT OUR MASTER CAME FROM LAODICEA, AND R. YOSE SON OF R. YEHUDAH AND R. ELAZAR SON OF YEHUDAH ENTERED AND SAT BEFORE HIM; HE SAID TO THEM: DRAW NEAR — I MUST BE GRATEFUL TO YOU THAT YOU WILL UPHOLD THE TORAH AFTER ME; YOU TOO MUST BE GRATEFUL TO YOUR CHILDREN THAT THEY WILL UPHOLD THE TORAH AFTER YOU. IF MOSES WERE NOT GREAT, AND HAD OTHERS NOT RECEIVED THE TORAH THROUGH HIM, IT WOULD NOT HAVE BEEN WORTH IT — [WE], HOW MUCH MORE. THEREFORE IT IS SAID "WHICH YOU SHALL COMMAND YOUR CHILDREN". ({SP_(335, 2, "צריך", "אני", "להחזיק", "לכם", "טובה")} "I must be grateful to you"; {SP_(335, 2, "מעשה", "שבא", "רבינו", "מלדיקיא")} "it happened that our Master came from Laodicea"): THE CHAIN OF TEACHING — the teacher\'s gratitude to the disciples who carry the Torah on (R. Yehudah the Patriarch; the translator: "sons" for disciples, piska 34); the last row of the piska; no law (DV32A-02). Fresh.')
srow(336, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR IT IS NO EMPTY THING FROM YOU" (32:47) — YOU HAVE NO EMPTY THING IN THE TORAH WHICH, IF YOU EXPOUND IT, HAS NO GIVING OF REWARD IN THIS WORLD WHILE THE PRINCIPAL STANDS FOR HIM FOR THE WORLD TO COME. KNOW THAT IT IS SO: THEY SAID, WHY IS IT WRITTEN "AND LOTAN\'S SISTER WAS TIMNA" (Genesis 36:22), "AND TIMNA WAS A CONCUBINE" (Genesis 36:12)? BECAUSE SHE SAID: I AM NOT WORTHY TO BE HIS WIFE, LET ME BE HIS CONCUBINE — AND ALL THIS WHY? TO MAKE KNOWN THE LOVE OF ABRAHAM OUR FATHER, THAT THERE WERE THOSE WHO WOULD NOT HAVE KINGSHIP AND RULE AND RAN TO CLEAVE TO HIM; AND IS IT NOT AN ARGUMENT FROM THE LIGHTER? IF ESAU, WHO HAD IN HIS HAND ONLY ONE COMMANDMENT, THAT HE HONORED HIS FATHER, KINGS AND RULERS RAN TO CLEAVE TO HIM — HOW MUCH MORE WOULD THEY RUN TO CLEAVE TO JACOB THE RIGHTEOUS, WHO UPHELD THE WHOLE TORAH, AS IT IS SAID "AND JACOB WAS A PERFECT MAN, DWELLING IN TENTS" (Genesis 25:27). The head row of piska 336 ({SP_(336, 1, "אין", "לך", "דבר", "ריקם", "בתורה")} "you have no empty thing in the Torah"; {SP_(336, 1, "והקרן", "קימת", "לו", "לעולם", "הבא")} "and the principal stands for him for the world to come"; {SP_(336, 1, "להודיעך", "חבתו", "של", "אברהם", "אבינו")} "to make known the love of Abraham our father"): THE FRUIT AND THE PRINCIPAL — Mishnah Peah 1:1\'s frame inside the spine (the translator: also Tosefta Peah 1:1-2; the testing shelf not opened); Timna\'s two verses on the tape (Genesis 36:12, 36:22 — the Genesis ledgers\' RUN CITATIONS) the proof that no verse is empty; Esau\'s one commandment (the honoring of his father) against Jacob\'s whole Torah (312:1\'s "perfect"); no law (DV32A-02). Fresh.')
srow(336, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THROUGH THIS THING YOU SHALL PROLONG DAYS" (32:47) — THIS IS ONE OF THE THINGS WHOSE DOER EATS THEIR FRUIT IN THIS WORLD AND HAS LENGTH OF DAYS IN THE WORLD TO COME; AND IT IS EXPLICIT HERE OF TORAH STUDY; OF HONORING FATHER AND MOTHER, WHENCE? THE TEACHING SAYS "HONOR YOUR FATHER AND YOUR MOTHER, THAT YOUR DAYS MAY BE LONG" (Exodus 20:12); OF SENDING AWAY THE NEST IT IS WRITTEN "YOU SHALL SURELY LET THE MOTHER GO AND TAKE THE YOUNG FOR YOURSELF, THAT IT MAY BE WELL WITH YOU AND YOU MAY PROLONG DAYS" (22:7); OF BRINGING PEACE IT IS WRITTEN "AND ALL YOUR CHILDREN SHALL BE TAUGHT OF THE LORD, AND GREAT SHALL BE THE PEACE OF YOUR CHILDREN" (Isaiah 54:13). ({SP_(336, 2, "ומפרש", "כאן", "בתלמוד", "תורה")} "and it is explicit here of Torah study"; {SP_(336, 2, "בשלוח", "הקן", "כתוב")} "of sending away the nest it is written"; {SP_(336, 2, "בהבאת", "שלום", "כתוב")} "of bringing peace it is written"): THE ANSWER SHEET INSIDE THE SPINE — Mishnah Peah 1:1\'s list (honoring parents, bringing peace, Torah study) each given its verse, with the nest added (the translator\'s note: the Sifrei weaves a companion to the Mishnah); 22:7\'s nest — the ledger deu_22_25\'s row, the nest law compiled at 17b (persons_poor_court — a REFERENCE); Exodus 20:12 on the tape a RUN CITATION; the last row of the piska; the compile: the reward\'s two arms — the fruit here, the days there (DV32A-02). REREAD WHOLE (chapters 22-25\'s reading — 22:7; the ledger deu_22_25).')
srow(337, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE LORD SPOKE TO MOSES IN THE SELFSAME DAY" (32:48) — IN THREE PLACES "IN THE SELFSAME DAY" IS SAID. IT IS SAID "IN THE SELFSAME DAY" OF NOAH (Genesis 7:13) — THIS TEACHES THAT NOAH\'S GENERATION WERE SAYING: BY SUCH-AND-SUCH, IF WE FEEL HIM AT IT WE WILL NOT LET HIM, AND MORE — WE WILL TAKE AXES AND HATCHETS AND SPLIT THE ARK ON HIM; THE HOLY ONE SAID: I BRING HIM IN AT MIDDAY, AND WHOEVER HAS POWER TO PROTEST, LET HIM COME AND PROTEST. AND WHY DID IT SEE FIT TO SAY OF EGYPT "IN THE SELFSAME DAY ALL THE HOSTS OF THE LORD WENT OUT" (Exodus 12:41)? BECAUSE THE EGYPTIANS WERE SAYING: BY SUCH-AND-SUCH, IF WE FEEL THEM AT IT WE WILL NOT LET THEM, AND MORE — WE WILL TAKE SWORDS AND BLADES AND KILL THEM; THE HOLY ONE SAID: I BRING THEM OUT AT MIDDAY, AND WHOEVER HAS POWER TO PROTEST, LET HIM COME AND PROTEST. AND WHY DID IT SEE FIT TO SAY HERE "IN THE SELFSAME DAY"? BECAUSE ISRAEL WERE SAYING: BY SUCH-AND-SUCH, IF WE FEEL HIM AT IT WE WILL NOT LET HIM — THE MAN WHO BROUGHT US OUT OF EGYPT AND SPLIT THE SEA FOR US AND BROUGHT DOWN THE MANNA FOR US AND BROUGHT THE QUAIL FOR US AND DID MIRACLES AND MIGHTY DEEDS FOR US, WE WILL NOT LET HIM; THE HOLY ONE SAID: I BRING HIM INTO THE CAVE AT MIDDAY, AND WHOEVER HAS POWER TO PROTEST, LET HIM COME AND PROTEST. THEREFORE IT IS SAID "AND THE LORD SPOKE TO MOSES IN THE SELFSAME DAY, SAYING". The one row of piska 337 ({SP_(337, 1, "בשלשה", "מקומות", "נאמר", "בעצם", "היום", "הזה")} "in three places: in the selfsame day is said"; {SP_(337, 1, "הריני", "מכניסו", "בחצי", "היום")} "I bring him in at midday"; {SP_(337, 1, "הריני", "מכניסו", "למערה", "בחצי", "היום")} "I bring him into the cave at midday"): THE MEASURE\'S KIN TAUGHT — 32:48 with Genesis 7:13 (the ark\'s boarding, the Genesis ledger\'s row) and Exodus 12:41 (the exodus\'s day on the tape, a RUN CITATION; the measure found 12:17, the spine\'s own seat 12:41 — the English cites 12:17): the eleven "selfsame day" of the Torah narrowed to the three where a protest is dared, "at midday" the answer; the cave the burial\'s (34:6 ahead — cited, not read); the compile: the aftermath\'s day the marker\'s (40, 12, 7) at 20b, the divine frame\'s one "saying" (DV32A-03). REREAD WHOLE (the Genesis ledger gen_17_boarding — Genesis 7:13).')
srow(338, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"GO UP INTO THIS MOUNTAIN OF ABARIM" (32:49) — IT IS AN ASCENT FOR YOU AND NOT A DESCENT. The head row of piska 338 ({SP_(338, 1, "עליה", "היא", "לך", "ואינה", "ירידה")} "it is an ascent for you and not a descent"): death as ascent; no law (DV32A-03). Fresh.')
srow(338, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"THIS MOUNTAIN OF ABARIM" (32:49) — WHICH IS CALLED BY FOUR NAMES: THE MOUNTAIN OF ABARIM, MOUNT NEBO, HOR THE MOUNTAIN, THE TOP OF PISGAH; AND WHY DO THEY CALL IT MOUNT NEBO? BECAUSE THREE PROPHETS WHO DIED NOT BY THE HAND OF TRANSGRESSION ARE BURIED IN IT, AND THESE ARE THEY: MOSES, AARON AND MIRIAM. ({SP_(338, 2, "שנקרא", "ארבעה", "שמות")} "which is called by four names"; {SP_(338, 2, "משה", "אהרן", "ומרים")} "Moses, Aaron and Miriam"): THE FOUR NAMES — Abarim, Nebo, Hor, Pisgah one mountain (the translator: Abarim read as "four", arba; Nebo as "prophets", nevi\'im); the spine\'s own identification of Hor the mountain (Aaron\'s, Numbers 20:22-28 on the tape) with Nebo — the teacher\'s link, carried as the shelf gives it; the three who died without transgression\'s hand (Miriam\'s death Numbers 20:1 on the tape — RUN CITATIONS); no law (DV32A-03). Fresh.')
srow(338, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHICH IS IN THE LAND OF MOAB" (32:49) — THIS TEACHES THAT HE SHOWED HIM THE CHAIN OF KINGS WHO ARE TO ARISE FROM RUTH THE MOABITESS; "WHICH IS OVER AGAINST JERICHO" — THIS TEACHES THAT HE SHOWED HIM THE CHAIN OF PROPHETS WHO ARE TO ARISE FROM RAHAB THE HARLOT; "AND SEE ALL THE LAND OF CANAAN" — R. ELIEZER SAYS: THE FINGER OF THE HOLY ONE WAS A GUIDE FOR MOSES AND SHOWED HIM ALL THE CITIES OF THE LAND OF ISRAEL: TO HERE EPHRAIM\'S BORDER, TO HERE MANASSEH\'S BORDER; R. YEHOSHUA SAYS: MOSES HIMSELF SAW IT — HOW? HE GAVE STRENGTH TO MOSES\' EYES AND HE SAW FROM THE END OF THE WORLD TO ITS END. ({SP_(338, 3, "שלשלת", "המלכים", "שעתידים", "לעמד", "מרות", "המואביה")} "the chain of kings who are to arise from Ruth the Moabitess"; {SP_(338, 3, "אצבעו", "של", "הקדוש", "ברוך", "הוא")} "the finger of the Holy One"; {SP_(338, 3, "משה", "בעצמו", "ראה", "אותה")} "Moses himself saw it"): THE SIGHT OF THE LAND OPENED TO ITS HISTORY — Ruth\'s kings and Rahab\'s prophets (the Writings\' and the Prophets\' seats cited, never read); the guide (metatron, "a guide" — the translator: not the named angel); the eyes strengthened; the last row of the piska; the compile: 34:1-4\'s sight AHEAD — cited, not read (DV32A-03). Fresh.')
